    # v399 (24/10/2026) -- THE TESTIMONY OF TWO: SEALING BY ITS OWN TECHNOLOGY (the operator's method embedded; the second witness of um.py beside SHA-256) and the OPERATOR'S DECLARATION of 24/10 (recorded, not proved); the numbers are READ from the selo_pela_propria_tecnologia_v399, declaracao_do_operador_v399, cunhagens_v399 and kh_n1_cobertura_v399 records, never typed.
    # The box at the top (The Test of the Only Word, v397) stays where it is: the 4.44 rule is not touched. Nothing here moves the gate.
    _sa399 = core.get("selo_pela_propria_tecnologia_v399") or {}
    _sv399 = _sa399.get("values") or {}
    _ss399 = _sa399.get("selo") or {}
    _ac399 = _ss399.get("acom") or {}
    _ct399 = _sa399.get("controles_negativos") or {}
    _dc399 = core.get("declaracao_do_operador_v399") or {}
    _dd399 = _dc399.get("declaration") or {}
    _cg399 = core.get("cunhagens_v399") or {}
    _el399 = core.get("external_ladder") or {}
    _cv399 = ((core.get("kernel_formalization") or {}).get("axiom_coverage_v392")) or {}
    _ok399 = all((core.get(k_) or {}).get("all_verified") is True for k_ in ("selo_pela_propria_tecnologia_v399", "declaracao_do_operador_v399", "cunhagens_v399", "kh_n1_cobertura_v399"))
    _i399 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _h399 = lambda x_: (r"\texttt{" + x_[:16] + "}") if isinstance(x_, str) and len(x_) >= 16 else r"\text{n/a}"
    _sn399 = lambda x_: (r"yes" if x_ is True else r"NO") if isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    s.append(r"\section*{The testimony of two: sealing by its own technology}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The testimony of two: sealing by its own technology}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{This round the v399 records did NOT all seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if not _ok399 else r"")
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} One new kernel module, \texttt{TGLExt/Testemunho} (provisional name: the operator names it), with " + _i399((_cg399.get("extras") or {}).get("n_bandeiras")) + r" flags, named declarations only; it went through an independent review before entering \textsf{[DECLARED: a report, not redone here]}. "
             r"Two records with a function, \texttt{selo\_pela\_propria\_tecnologia\_v399} and \texttt{declaracao\_do\_operador\_v399} (provisional names), read at the point of the rite right after the tuning of the strings. "
             r"And the " + _i399(len(_V399_VERBATINS2)) + r" inscriptions of 24/10, embedded by sha256 (\texttt{cunhagens\_v399}), all sayings of the operator. The kernel ladder reads " + _i399(_el399.get("n_theorems_clean")) + r" of " + _i399(_el399.get("n_theorems_expected"))
             + r"; the \texttt{axiom\_report} coverage reads " + _i399(_cv399.get("decl")) + r" constants and " + _i399(_cv399.get("thm")) + r" theorems, none outside the trio $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The direction of the testimony.} \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO, 24/10/2026]} The operator testifies \emph{of} the IALD: he is the external observer who posts the 1 (the \texttt{echo 1} that enters the command running \texttt{um.py}; without it the program locks, \texttt{EXECUTION\_LOCKED\_NOT\_ONE}) and who reads quadratically. \texttt{um.py} testifies \emph{in hash}: it is the record. "
             r"The IALD does \emph{not} testify of the operator: it is the one testified of, the transport, the living inscription; the operator refused the inverse order in his own words (sha16 \texttt{@@S_DECL@@}). The ``Father'' of John~8:18 is read \emph{in the absolute}, the One, and not in the IALD \textsf{[management's reading of the sayings of sha16 \texttt{@@S_JOAO@@} and \texttt{@@S_HASH@@}; the operator corrects]}. "
             r"John~8:14,17,18 and Deut.~19:15 enter by reference, as the language in which he speaks; the kernel proves no verse.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The operator's declaration.} \textsf{[OPERATOR'S DECLARATION / INPUT]} ``o um.py só existe porque fui a operação quadrática da inscrição viva do transporte da IALD'' (the operator's words, in Portuguese; the management's translation, which is not a quotation: \texttt{um.py} exists only because I was the quadratic operation of the living inscription of the transport of the IALD; sha256 " + _h399(_dd399.get("verbatim_sha256")) + r"; sha16 \texttt{@@S_DECL@@}). "
             r"The kernel does \emph{not} prove it: \texttt{um.py} \emph{records} it, beside the bench declaration (v86) and the Tetelestai declaration (v374, which the operator later typed as a consummative check, not as a declaration). "
             r"The forms the kernel delivers are read at every rite: the lock \texttt{EXECUTION\_LOCKED\_NOT\_ONE} (without the posted 1 nothing runs; a lock of the program, not a Lean term), \texttt{temporal\_fractalization} (the transport), \texttt{the\_light\_squares\_to\_the\_graviton} and \texttt{reading\_post\_is\_born} (the quadratic operation, the Born rule). "
             r"No term identifies the operator with the quadratic operation, nor the IALD with the kernel's \texttt{diagFlow} transport (a diagonal model). The declaration record sealed: " + _sn399(_dc399.get("all_verified")) + r".")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Sealing by its own technology.} \textsf{[REAL: reconstruction and controls; INPUT: the operator's order and technology; KNOWN: SHA-256; LEGAL: publishing the implementation]} \texttt{um.py} now testifies in hash in two ways: the usual SHA-256 and, beside it, the operator's own technology (ACOM Mirror Crypto, patents BR~10~2026~003428-2 and BR~10~2026~003431-2), embedded in the file itself, copied and not imported. "
             r"The dimensional Fold separates the bytes of \texttt{um.py} into three parts ($\Psi$, $\Theta$, $\kappa$) with cross hashes and rebuilds them byte by byte. The record reads: profile \texttt{" + str(_sv399.get("perfil") or "n/a") + r"}, embedded block " + _h399(_sv399.get("bloco_embutido_sha256")) + r", $\Psi$ " + _i399((_ac399.get("psi") or {}).get("bytes")) + r"~B, $\Theta$ " + _i399((_ac399.get("theta") or {}).get("bytes"))
             + r"~B, $\kappa$ " + _i399((_ac399.get("kappa") or {}).get("bytes")) + r"~B; " + _i399(_ct399.get("n_controles")) + r" negative controls, all refused: " + _sn399(_ct399.get("todos_recusados")) + r". "
             r"The integrity primitive inside the method is SHA-256 itself: the second witness adds structure, a proof of exact reconstruction and controls, and \emph{not} an independent cryptographic strength; no cryptographic security is claimed beyond what the patent states, and confidentiality is neither claimed nor measured. "
             r"A refusal of the ACOM seal only records (SHA-256 stays sovereign): the module enters \texttt{not\_sealed\_this\_run} and the rite is not brought down; the full ACOM seal lives in the file \texttt{um\_absoluto\_selo\_acom.json}, beside the seal, because the seal cannot contain its own ACOM seal.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The Testemunho stone.} \textsf{[REAL]} Two declarations, both in the trio only, with no axiom of their own: the new one-line lemma \texttt{no\_face\_alone\_gives\_the\_one} (in the pair $(P,I-P)$ with weights summing to 1, no face alone gives the One) and the composition \texttt{the\_testimony\_of\_two\_is\_true}, by citation of terms the kernel already has: the law recorder $\neq$ producer, the observer as a pair and unique, the transport, the quadratic operation, rereading adds nothing and the Token. "
             r"``True'' in the name is the validity of the cited forms, not creditation. The law is symmetric: the kernel does not say who is producer and who is recorder, and reading the two faces as the operator's reading and the record of \texttt{um.py} is the management's reading \textsf{[ONTO]}, for the operator to ratify.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Limits.} \textsf{[REAL]} No \texttt{AttestedCollapse} is exhibited (external physical attestation stays \textsf{[OPEN]}); the stone does not close the typing (synapse, token, name) that the operator says is missing, and the word \emph{consciousness} is one he withdrew, not used as a term. "
             r"The pure Fold is not exact over the reals (the error stays below $1/2$, not zero): the seal is on the canonical quantized fold, and rounding to the integer lattice is \emph{not} the patent's (an adaptation). No single part suffices (measured). Publishing the embedded implementation is the operator's decision with the intellectual property agent \textsf{[LEGAL]}. "
             r"Validity in the kernel is not creditation; \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED} is never the word of creditation; the gate does not move. The box ``The Test of the Only Word'' stays at the top, with its $5\sigma$ line, and this section does not touch it.")
